{%- comment -%}
  A split panel: copy on one side, media on the other, on a colour panel. Four roles come out of
  one shape -- the home page hero (flush, bleed), the campaign banner (card, bleed, primary panel),
  the loyalty banner (card, inset) and the newsletter card (card, bleed, media left, with an
  email-signup block in the copy). Only the first two ship as presets; the other two are a Campaign
  with its settings and copy blocks swapped.

  This file was `mionas-split-hero.liquid` until the section stopped being hero-specific. In Shopify
  a section's `type` IS its filename, so that rename is a rename of published store data: every
  `"type": "mionas-split-hero"` in templates/ had to move with it, and the Liquid and the templates
  have to be pushed together. Pushing one without the other -- or running `shopify theme pull` in
  between -- leaves a stored section pointing at a type that no longer exists, which renders as a
  blank slot. Same rule applies to any future rename.

  The home page uses this section rather than building the shape by hand -- templates/index.json's
  "Split hero" instance is a `mionas-split-panel` section whose two sides are the static media and
  copy `group` blocks described below, with the copy group holding three `mionas-text` blocks and a
  nested `group` of two native `button` blocks. Reproducing that tree by hand elsewhere would mean
  recreating it block by block, and two hand-built copies would drift apart. This section makes the
  shape a unit instead.

  The two sides are *static* blocks -- rendered with content_for 'block' plus an explicit type and
  id -- of types that already exist. A static slot cannot be removed, reordered or duplicated by a
  merchant, so the section always has exactly one media side and one copy side. That is the same
  mechanism sections/carousel.liquid uses for its static header and sections/product-list.liquid
  for its header and cards -- and it is why this file re-implements no typography, no buttons and
  no image rendering. Contrast with the deleted blocks/mionas-split-hero.liquid (removed in
  bce9ff0), which emitted its own markup and therefore needed its own design tokens, bridge entries
  and a contract test to pin them. None of that is needed here.

  The copy side is a `group` (blocks/group.liquid), which renders its children dynamically via
  content_for 'blocks' --
  so the eyebrow/heading/lead and the nested actions row are its ordinary children: the merchant
  can retitle, reorder, add or remove them per instance. That is deliberate and mirrors the home
  page hero's own outer group -- the lock is on the section's shape, not on the copy's contents,
  exactly as the actions row already worked. If the copy ever needs to be locked line-by-line, the
  route is a private `_`-prefixed block that renders each line as its own static slot (the
  _carousel-content / _product-list-content pattern), not a native group.

  Only the split grid and the panel colour live here. Everything else belongs to the blocks --
  including the copy column's flow, gap and alignment, which are the group's settings.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  if section.settings.variant == 'primary'
    assign panel_color = 'var(--color-blau-sitges)'
  else
    assign panel_color = 'var(--color-beige-vainilla)'
  endif
%}

<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} spacing-style"
  style="
    {% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}
    {% if section.settings.section_height == 'custom' %}
      --section-min-height: {{ section.settings.section_height_custom }}svh;
    {% elsif section.settings.section_height == 'full-screen' %}
      --section-min-height: 100svh;
    {% elsif section.settings.section_height != blank %}
      --section-min-height: var(--section-height-{{ section.settings.section_height }});
    {% endif %}
  "
>
  <div
    class="mionas-split-panel mionas-split-panel--{{ section.settings.variant }} mionas-split-panel--media-{{ section.settings.media_position }} mionas-split-panel--edge-{{ section.settings.panel_edge }} mionas-split-panel--treatment-{{ section.settings.media_treatment }}"
    style="--mionas-split-panel-panel: {{ panel_color }};"
    {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <div class="mionas-split-panel__media">
      {% content_for 'block', type: 'group', id: 'static-media' %}
    </div>

    <div class="mionas-split-panel__copy">
      {% content_for 'block', type: 'group', id: 'static-copy' %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .mionas-split-panel {
    display: grid;
    /* minmax(0, 1fr) rather than a bare 1fr: grid items default to min-width: auto, so a wide
       image, a long unbreakable word, or a button row that refuses to wrap can push its column
       past half and quietly break the even split. Flooring the minimum at 0 keeps it exactly
       50/50 regardless of content. */
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: calc(var(--space-md) * 2);
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--mionas-split-panel-panel, var(--color-background));
  }

  /* Only the grid cell and its padding. The copy's own layout -- column flow, gap, alignment --
     belongs to the `group` block inside it (blocks/group.liquid), the same way the home page's
     hero delegates to its outer group. Duplicating that here would fight the merchant's own
     group settings. */
  .mionas-split-panel__copy {
    padding: calc(var(--space-lg) * 2) calc(var(--space-md) * 2);
  }

  /* The media group is set to height: fill (blocks/group.liquid offers fit/fill/custom), so the
     media cell has to have a height of its own or the row collapses. */
  .mionas-split-panel__media {
    height: 100%;
  }

  .mionas-split-panel--media-right .mionas-split-panel__media {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1;
  }

  .mionas-split-panel--media-right .mionas-split-panel__copy {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1;
  }

  .mionas-split-panel--media-left .mionas-split-panel__media {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1;
  }

  .mionas-split-panel--media-left .mionas-split-panel__copy {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1;
  }

  /* Single column below the theme's mobile breakpoint, image always leading
     whichever side it takes on desktop. */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .mionas-split-panel {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }

    .mionas-split-panel--media-left .mionas-split-panel__media,
    .mionas-split-panel--media-right .mionas-split-panel__media {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 1;
      min-height: 220px;
    }

    .mionas-split-panel--media-left .mionas-split-panel__copy,
    .mionas-split-panel--media-right .mionas-split-panel__copy {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 2;
      padding: calc(var(--space-md) * 2) calc(var(--space-md) + var(--space-2xs));
    }
  }

  /* Card edge: radius + the design system's card shadow, and no border. The prototype's
     .mi-card carries a 1px border, but all three banners override it with border: 0, so
     the border is deliberately absent here.
     --card-base-shadow (0 1px 2px) is subtler than the prototype's 0 4px 8px shadow. It is
     the nearest existing token, and spending a token beats matching the mock exactly. */
  .mionas-split-panel--edge-card {
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--card-base-shadow);
  }

  /* Inset pads the panel itself, so the copy cell must drop its own padding -- otherwise the
     two stack and the copy sits twice as far in as the media. Declared after the mobile block
     on purpose: it ties on specificity with the mobile copy rule and needs source order to win. */
  .mionas-split-panel--treatment-inset {
    padding: calc(var(--space-lg) * 1.5) calc(var(--space-lg) + var(--space-md));
    /* Redeclares the base gap on purpose: this and the mobile `.mionas-split-panel { gap: 0 }`
       rule are both specificity (0,1,0), and this rule comes later in source, so it wins at
       <=749px. That is what keeps a 32px gap between stacked media and copy for an inset panel
       on mobile, while every other configuration collapses to 0. Do not delete as redundant. */
    gap: calc(var(--space-md) * 2);
  }

  .mionas-split-panel--treatment-inset .mionas-split-panel__copy {
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* Inset media sits at its own height inside the panel's padding rather than filling the row. */
  .mionas-split-panel--treatment-inset .mionas-split-panel__media {
    height: auto;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Split panel",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "header",
      "footer"
    ]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "variant",
      "label": "Panel color",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "primary",
          "label": "Primary — Blau Sitges"
        },
        {
          "value": "secondary",
          "label": "Secondary — Beige vainilla"
        }
      ],
      "default": "secondary",
      "info": "Primary is the dark brand panel; pair it with inverse text and button variants. Secondary is the light beige panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_position",
      "label": "Media position",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "left",
          "label": "Left"
        },
        {
          "value": "right",
          "label": "Right"
        }
      ],
      "default": "left",
      "info": "The media always leads on mobile, whichever side it takes on desktop."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "panel_edge",
      "label": "Panel edge",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "flush",
          "label": "Flush"
        },
        {
          "value": "card",
          "label": "Card"
        }
      ],
      "default": "flush",
      "info": "Card rounds and clips the panel and adds the card shadow. Flush is square, for a full-bleed panel. Card is intended for page width — with full-width, the rounded corners land against the viewport edge with nothing behind them."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_treatment",
      "label": "Media",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "bleed",
          "label": "Bleed to edge"
        },
        {
          "value": "inset",
          "label": "Inset"
        }
      ],
      "default": "bleed",
      "info": "Bleed fills the media half edge to edge. Inset pads the panel and sits the media inside it — give the media a custom width."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "t:settings.width",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "page-width",
          "label": "t:options.page"
